Add safe local refresh and test rejected data — learner brief
Fictional Northstar Services training material.
Refresh
Replace-only local JSON import. Validate entire candidate: required fields, numeric amounts, one valid period, unique keys, EAST/WEST, USD. Reject duplicate/missing actual/EUR; preserve last valid state. Empty data explicit.
Task
The next period's data should replace the September view only if the whole file passes validation.
Actions
	1	Specify replace-only refresh and all-or-nothing validation.
	2	Ask AI to add local JSON file selection with validation of keys, required numeric fields, currency, and period consistency.
	3	Load the valid October fixture and confirm two rows and 220/220/0.
	4	Try each invalid variant and verify that an explanatory error appears while October remains the current valid dataset.
	5	Check that the displayed period and row count always match the last valid data.
	6	Record the refresh limitation: local-only, no live integration.
Output
Refresh contract; revised source; valid/invalid test results; last-valid-state evidence; data-status label.
Supplied local practice files
	•	dashboard-starter.html
	•	invalid-currency.json
	•	invalid-duplicate.json
	•	invalid-missing.json
	•	october.json
	•	september.json
Keep these files together. Scripts take explicit paths; choose new output folders. Use a plain text editor to inspect source before running. Browser prototypes open locally; do not deploy them.
